I finished the research stage for sombr and wrote `evidence.json` to the run folder. It passes the pipeline's own validator, and I didn't change or publish anything else.

**The call:** this is an **open case**, not a confident typing.
- **Leading read:** Type 3, at low confidence.
- **Main rival:** Type 4.
- **Also in play:** Type 7.

The stage name says "somber," but his behavior points elsewhere:
- **Ambition stated early:** at 18, with no hit, he told a magazine Madison Square Garden was his dream: "but it will happen. I know it!" He now plays two nights there on November 23–24. On Fallon in June, after the shows were booked, he said his life goal had been "a 1,000-seater."
- **Audience-tested songs:** he posts a song's chorus on TikTok first and only finishes the ones that get a response.
- **What he fears:** being dropped by his label, being "a disappointment," and having "not performed well" for fans.
- **Feeling good via others:** in his childhood bedroom he told CBS he never felt good at anything "until other people told me that I was good."

The Four case is just as consistent. He describes years of intense emotion, writes alone because it feels too vulnerable to do otherwise, and fights his producer to keep rough bedroom vocals. Nothing in the record yet separates the two. The real test is how he handles a commercial setback or a choice between pop and his "roots," and his second album isn't announced.

**What the record is:**
- 38 sources opened, including about three and a half hours of transcribed interviews.
- 45 sourced claims.
- Testimony comes only from friends, collaborators and admirers (Taylor Swift, Lindsey Buckingham, Quenlin Blackwell, Inde Navarrette).

**Sensitive material:** his reviewers will be the full six-person jury, both because open cases require it and because of what the record contains:
- A TikTok critic's claims about his concert banter in front of young fans.
- "Industry plant" accusations tied to his father's events company.
- His own disclosures about depression, anxiety attacks, eating and body image.

The file tells the drafter to quote all of this only in his words, never as type evidence, and never as the hook.

**Caveats:**
- Most quotes come from auto-captions, so each needs checking against the audio before it's printed.
- The backlog note about "possible Grammy noms Nov 16" couldn't be verified, so it's marked do-not-print.
- The case is set to be reopened on December 15, after the Garden shows.
